Temam babo, em noke da rin mala xalê Elî.
 
Okay man, we are now going to Uncle Ali's house.

155
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Tebeqîzîk jironî me jî da biro.
 
A lower layer/road also took us.

156
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:32,000
Em ê fitilekê cemo ra darboz bin.
 
We will pass a turn near them.

157
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Hindik mandik ma maykê me bi megîne.
 
A tiny bit remained [it was close] that our microphone got
caught.

158
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:31,000
As salam aleykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

159
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Kakê tu çawayî?
 
Brother, how are you?

160
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Başî?
 
Are you good?

161
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:48,000
Spas.
 
Thanks.

162
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Are xokê ma, mala we li qolî ta ye.
 
Oh our sister, your house is at the very peak/end.

163
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:56,000
Em hatine hewşê ginde.
 
We have come to the village yard.

164
00:27:56,000 --> 00:28:02,000
Maşallah cewkî pir xoş e hewalî ma werda.
 
Mashallah, the atmosphere is very nice, bring our friend
here.

165
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Taben vê darê tirkê ber kexoyte...
 
Naturally, this tree has put out [fruit]...

166
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Mantiqok pir xoş e.
 
It is a very nice logic [view].

167
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,000
Hîn pîşê dar e, hîn xoş e.
 
It is in front of the tree, it is nicer.

168
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:14,000
Pir bilind e.
 
It is very high up.

169
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Keremke şîratî, keremke şîratî, keremke.
 
Welcome to the advice/gathering, welcome to the gathering,
please come in.

170
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:38,000
Emê noke hontî tilit a bikin, em hatin mala we jî.
 
We will now make a... [slang], we came to your house too.

171
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Ez mehirê te dernxînim berîkê.
 
I won't take your dowry out of the pocket.

172
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:43,000
Paş neyê, xolî mîj e were.
 
Don't come later, come while it is dusty/foggy [come
immediately].

173
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Baş e, nuh xolî mîj e ware.
 
Okay, now that it is dusty/foggy, I will come.

174
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Tobe, qebûl kin, em mêvanê xwedê ne, qebûl kin.
 
Repentance [Please], accept us, we are guests of God, accept
us.

175
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,000
Ser ser û ser çava.
 
You are welcome [Upon head and eyes].

176
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:53,000
Keremke.
 
Please come in.

177
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Cewkî xoş e.
 
The weather is nice.

178
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:57,000
Hênik e, dorê me tî ye.
 
It is cool, our surroundings are mulberry trees.

179
00:28:57,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Maniskim xo fîsta.
 
I won't dip myself... [slang].

180
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Cemaetî me, like û iştiraq bîr neken.
 
Our community, don't forget to like and subscribe.

181
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:13,000
Sihet xweş?
 
Is the health good?

182
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Spas, spas.
 
Thanks, thanks.

183
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Me te nas kir?
 
Did we recognize you?

184
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:17,000
Tu çawayî?
 
How are you?

185
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Ez pîr bûme, ez ne pîr bûme?
 
I have become old, haven't I become old?

186
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Na na, tu gellekî ciwan î.
 
No no, you are very young.

187
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Ez pîr bûme.
 
I have become old.

188
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Tu gellekî ciwan î, maşallah.
 
You are very young, Mashallah.

189
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:27,000
Keremke.
 
Please come in.

190
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Tu çawayî?
 
How are you?

191
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Keremkin, keremkin.
 
Welcome, welcome.

192
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:37,000
Bi xêr hatin, ser çava.
 
Welcome, upon my eyes [thank you].

193
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Bi xêr hatin.
 
Welcome.

194
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,000
Ser çava.
 
Upon my eyes [Thanks].

195
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Bas min bîr neken.
 
Just don't forget me.

196
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Bêjin like û abone.
 
Say like and subscribe.

197
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Bêjin like.
 
Say like.

198
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Bêjin like.
 
Say like.

199
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,000
Mantiqok pir xoş e.
 
It is a very nice logic [view/vibe].

200
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:54,000
Hewa xoş e, ne?
 
The weather is nice, isn't it?

201
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Elhamdulillah bereket e.
 
Praise be to God, it is abundance.

202
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Hemd ji xwedê ra.
 
Thanks be to God.

203
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:03,000
Dîsa bereket be serdarê min.
 
May it be blessed again, my leader.

204
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Tu şîrîn î, xwedê te bihêle.
 
You are sweet, may God keep you.

205
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Tu sax bî, heyatê min, canê min.
 
May you be healthy, my life, my soul.

206
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:10,000
Em şa bûn bi hatina we tenê.
 
We were happy just by your arrival.

207
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Ye xwedê temena we dirêj bike inşallah.
 
May God grant you a long life, God willing.

208
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Ma tu keyfa xwe ji gund ra naynî?
 
Are you not enjoying the village?

209
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Welle dewr e no...
 
Well, it is the era/time no...

210
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Ka ji me ra bêje, ma ne te digot gund şîrîn e, tiştek nîne?
 
Tell us, didn't you say the village is sweet, and there is
nothing [like it]?

211
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Ax, wele pir şîrîn e, lê xerbatî jî çetîn e zate, xerbatî
îmanê li mero dişewitîne.
 
Ah, by God it is very sweet, but exile is also difficult
indeed, exile burns one's faith.

212
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:27,000
Wele, wele.
 
By God, by God.

213
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:31,000
Çiqas malê mero gundî, mero xirabe be, dîsa...
 
No matter how much one's home in the village is a ruin,
still...

214
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Heft heyşt sal e, em dûrî xerîbiyê bûn.
 
It's been seven or eight years, we were away in exile.

215
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Wele tiştekî wiha... xerbatî zor zor e.
 
By God, such a thing... exile is very, very hard.

216
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:38,000
Wele dîsa hem bikîf e, elhemdulillah.
 
By God, it is still enjoyable, praise be to God.

217
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Wele nanê tîr, tiştekî be...
 
By God, [even if it is] dry bread, or something [small]...

218
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Nanê tîr bi nanê tîr, baştir e ji kibabê xelqê çêtir e.
 
Dry bread with dry bread, it is better, better than the
kebab of strangers.

219
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:47,000
Ê tebhet, tebhet, tiştekî ekîd e.
 
Oh naturally, naturally, that is a certain thing.

220
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:48,000
Elhemdulillah, bereket be.
 
Praise be to God, may it be blessed.

221
00:30:48,000 --> 00:31:08,000
Elhemdulillah şikir.
 
Praise be to God, thanks.

222
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Xalû, ev mala kê ye, bera kî ta ye? Xaltîk?
 
Uncle, whose house is this, facing you? Auntie?

223
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:19,000
Ev mala... Rêdûr? Mala Rêdûr nabe.
 
This is the house of... Redur? It can't be Redur's house.

224
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Bavê Rêdûr.
 
Redur's father.

225
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Were noqta imkên şûşê, noqta, teswîr ke.
 
Come to the point where the glass [lens] can, to the point,
film it.

226
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:27,000
Ev cihê horta ye wey.
 
This is the place of the young men, oh my.

227
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:34,000
Maşallah malê we ra tolî gund e.
 
Mashallah, your houses are at the top of the village.

228
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Xalû mala kê ye?
 
Uncle, whose house is it?

229
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Mala Bavê Mihemed Nazmî, Bavê Mihemed.
 
The house of Mihemed Nazmi's father, Mihemed's father.

230
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Ew kulfeta wî jî, navê wê Beşîra ye.
 
And his wife, her name is Beshira.

231
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:47,000
Eywa. Xaltîka Beşîra, ev malbata te ye.
 
Aye. Auntie Beshira, this is your family [home].

232
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Eywa, ev yê hewşê Xwedê ye, ev yê hewşa Rêdîn e, berê xwe
bidê.
 
Aye, this one with the courtyard belongs to God [is ruined],
this is the courtyard of Redin, look at it.

233
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Abo, lî min, wer camê nanê li vir jî bigire.
 
Abo, listen to me, come capture the glass [view] of the
bread [oven?] here too.

234
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Ew jî mala Rêdîn e mero, blokê Bavê Mihemed e.
 
That is also Redin's house man, the block of Mihemed's
father.

235
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:59,000
Pir serî ye, ser çavê min.
 
Very highly [regarded], upon my eyes.

236
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:01,000
Xaltîk ma hûne tê dîtine, xaltîka min.
 
Auntie, are you seeing it, my auntie.

237
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Tev jî kevir e, ev ev malbata te ye tebhet.
 
It is all stone, this, this is your family [home] naturally.

238
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:09,000
Boka wî meke jî bira, wele bilindî ye, pir bilindî ye.
 
Don't zoom/focus on its side brother, by God it is a height,
a great height.

239
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Ev ê paş me jî mala pismamê gundî ye.
 
The one behind us is also the house of a cousin from the
village.

240
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:13,000
Ev ê paş me jî dotir mala pismamê te ye?
 
The one behind us is also your cousin's house?

241
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Mala Fewzî. Mala Fewzî.
 
Fewzi's house. Fewzi's house.

242
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Emê çêkin nuka.
 
We will do [film] it now.

243
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:17,000
Mala kê ye ew ê paş?
 
Whose house is that behind?

244
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Mala Sebrî. Ew jî pismamê Bavê Mihemed e.
 
Sabri's house. He is also the cousin of Mihemed's father.

245
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Eywa. Mala Sebrî ye.
 
Aye. It is Sabri's house.

246
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Pir serî me, ser çavê me.
 
Very highly [regarded] by us, upon our eyes.

247
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Were Abo lî min, li vir jî bigire leqtekê.
 
Come Abo, listen to me, take a shot here too.

248
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:33,000
Ev na malbata kê ne li rex xalê min?
 
Whose family is this next to my uncle?

249
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Ew cîranê me ne.
 
They are our neighbors.

250
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:36,000
Cîranê xwen e ne?
 
They are their neighbors, right?

251
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:38,000
Mala Cemîlê Beşîr ne gero.
 
It's Cemîlê Beşîr's house, presumably.

252
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Cemîlê Beşîr.
 
Cemîlê Beşîr.

253
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Maşallah mewqekî bilind e, pir xweş e. Bakî hênik lê ye.
 
Mashallah, it is a high location, very nice. A cool breeze
is upon it.

254
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:52,000
Erê hevalê min dibêje, ev mala tebhet hember me mala Mistefê
ye.
 
Yes my friend says, this house naturally opposite us is
Mistefe's house.

255
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Mala Mistefê ye.
 
It is Mistefe's house.

256
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:56,000
Bi laqabê wî Sebrî.
 
With his nickname Sabri.

257
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:59,000
Tebhet, ev horta waye û...
 
Naturally, this is their place [of the youth] and...

258
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Ew jî, wîş tê dîtin.
 
That as well, look, it can be seen.

259
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:03,000
Ser serî me, ser çavê me.
 
Upon our heads, upon our eyes.

260
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Ev jî horta gundî ye zate?
 
This is also the place of the village youth, indeed?

261
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Erê ev jî horta gundî ye.
 
Yes, this is also the place of the village youth.

262
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Ev jî mala Husênê Ehmedê Ganî bera dibêje, bawer bike wilo
ye.
 
This is also the house of Husein Ehmed Gani, he presumably
says, believe me it is so.

263
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:28,000
Denge. Wele mewqekî pir xweş e zîbaret.
 
Look. By God, it is a very nice location, the shrine.

264
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:36,000
Abo lî min, li leqtekê, axa noka, noka xelas bike.
 
Abo listen to me, [take] a shot, the land now, finish it
now.

265
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:41,000
Erê hevalno, tebhet inşallah ez ê miradê dilê giya bikim
xaltîk.
 
Yes friends, naturally, God willing I will fulfill the
desire of everyone's heart, Auntie.

266
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Ev horta te ye, gundê te ye, malbata te li vir nîne, meyrê
te ne tebhet.
 
This is your place, your village, your family is not here,
your husband is not [here] naturally.

267
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:48,000
Abo lî min, vê horta yekê bigire çikê.
 
Abo listen to me, take [a shot] of this place for a moment.

268
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Mewqekî pir bilind û xweş e.
 
It is a very high and nice location.

269
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Me ji xalû pirs kir, Kevrê Kar maneta xwe çi ye, xêr e ji vê
re Kevrê Kar?
 
We asked the uncle, what is the meaning of "Kevrê Kar" (The
Deaf Rock), why is it [called] The Deaf Rock here?

270
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:59,000
Dibê hemberî çokî bilind e.
 
He says opposite it is a very high bank/cliff.

271
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Tilvî yolî bişkinî, te bang ke, yolî din hes nake.
 
If you break/shout to the other side, [if] you call out, the
other side does not hear/sense.

272
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:05,000
Vî yolî, mesela te bang ke, yolî din hes nake.
 
[From] this side, for example if you call out, the other
side does not hear.

273
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Xêra vî re wî manê dibên Kevrê Kar.
 
For the sake of this meaning, they call it The Deaf Rock.

274
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,000
Deng nayê î din.
 
The voice does not come to the other [side].

275
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:12,000
Erê bra, bilindî ye xweş e.
 
Yes brother, it is a height, it is nice.

276
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Abo lî min leqtekê, ji wî horta jî bigire.
 
Abo listen to me, take a shot, take from that place as well.

277
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:33,000
Hema şû bye bye ke, hema şû bye bye ke.
 
Just do "bye-bye" [wave], just do "bye-bye".

278
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:34,000
Hema şû bye bye ke.
 
Just do "bye-bye".

279
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Esta berê te seltanet e berê te.
 
Now your direction is sovereignty/royalty, your direction.

280
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:43,000
Bye bye ke vêra, bye bye ke, a xaltîka, xaltîka re bye bye
ke.
 
Do "bye-bye" to here, do "bye-bye", ah to the auntie, do
"bye-bye" to the auntie.

281
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:47,000
Abo ca were li vî ciyî.
 
Abo come to this place here.

282
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Mêvanê xaltîka Siltanê ne.
 
We are guests of Auntie Sultan.

283
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,000
Bêje xaltîk, ma tu ça ye?
 
Say Auntie, how are you?

284
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Ê, keyfa min li ba ye.
 
Eh, my mood is good.

285
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Tu baş î? Siheta te xweş e?
 
Are you well? Is your health good?

286
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Ez baş im, hûn bixêr hatin.
 
I am well, you are welcome.

287
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:55,000
Li vê derê tu bi tenê yî?
 
Are you alone in this place?

288
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:57,000
Welle em li gund in.
 
By God, we are in the village.

289
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:59,000
We xwedê emrê te dirêj bike xaltîk.
 
May God prolong your life, Auntie.

290
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:01,000
Silavê min ji giya ra hene.
 
My greetings are to everyone.

291
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,000
Silavê te ji kî ra hene?
 
To whom are your greetings?

292
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:09,000
Ji Fatmê ra, ji Rozê ra, ji Avînê ra, ji Hemûdê ra, ji
Ehmed, ji Serserîme, ser çavê me.
 
To Fatima, to Roza, to Avin, to Hamude, to Ahmed, upon my
head, upon my eyes.

293
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:12,000
Sebrî jî, qîza dayîka min e.
 
Sabri as well, he is my mother's daughter's [son/relative?].

294
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:17,000
Emanetê xwa me, ehlen we sehlen, silavê min ji giya ra hene.
 
I entrust myself [to God], welcome, my greetings are to
everyone.

295
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Ser serî me.
 
Upon our heads.

296
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Silavê min ji Samîra jî, û ji keçikê me jî, ji... Mihemed
Elî ye, Mesûd Elî ye, Mistefa ye.
 
My greetings to Samira too, and to our girls too, to...
Mihemed Ali, Masud Ali, Mustafa.

297
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Emîra ye, Fatma ye.
 
Amira, Fatma.

298
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:32,000
Ehmed e, Welîd e, Hesen e, silavê min ji giya ra hene.
 
Ahmed, Walid, Hassan, my greetings are to everyone.

299
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Qîza min Semîra lî ye, Nûrîn lî ye, silavê min ji giya ra
hene.
 
My daughter Samira is there, Nureen is there, my greetings
are to everyone.

300
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:37,000
Silavê min ji Xelîl ra jî hene.
 
My greetings are to Khalil as well.

301
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Erebê, xaltîka, dotmamê.
 
The Arabs, the auntie, the female cousin.

302
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,000
Xwedê siheta we xweş bike.
 
May God give you good health.

303
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:45,000
Silavê min ji giya ra hene kurban, jê re bêje nêzîk, saetek
we xweş.
 
My greetings are to everyone, my dear, tell them [it will
be] soon, have a good time.

304
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:47,000
Bêje Başîra jî xweş.
 
Say Bashira is well too.

305
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:49,000
Ez li vir nakim, ez li şûnda me.
 
I don't do [live?] here, I am behind.

306
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Baş, xwedê emrê te dirêj bike xaltîk.
 
Good, may God prolong your life, Auntie.

307
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,000
Xwedê saeta we xweş ke.
 
May God make your time pleasant.

308
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Inşallah wekî tê bê, emê miradê dilê giya bikin.
 
God willing, as you say, we will fulfill the desire of
everyone's heart.

309
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:59,000
Maşallah xaltîka min xwedê emrê te dirêj bike de.
 
Mashallah, my auntie, may God give you a long life then.

310
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:02,000
Emî li malbata te digerin tebhet.
 
We are looking around your family [home], naturally.

311
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:08,000
Noha jî emê dakevin jî jêr, gundî me mala çêkin, tebhet
silavê ji gundî me mala, em dişînin ji wa ra.
 
And now we will go down below, we will film the village
